        -:   54:/**
        -:   55: * An 8 bit string that is assuredly encoded in UTF8, and supplies special conversion
        -:   56: * support to and from wxString, to and from std::string, and has non-mutating iteration
        -:   57: * over Unicode characters.
        -:   58: *
        -:   59: * I've been careful to supply only conversion facilities and not try and duplicate
        -:   60: * wxString() with many member functions. There are multiple ways to create text into
        -:   61: * a std::string without the need of too many member functions:
        -:   62: *
        -:   63: *  - std::ostringstream.
        -:   64: *
        -:   65: * Because this class uses no virtuals, it should be possible to cast any std::string
        -:   66: * into a UTF8 using this kind of cast: (UTF8 &) without construction or copying being
        -:   67: * the effect of the cast.  Be sure the source std::string holds UTF8 encoded text before
        -:   68: * you do that.
        -:   69: */
        -:   70:class UTF8
        -:   71:{
